title: Add pallet-pgas-allowance with ChargeFeeWithPgas transaction extension
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      - Introduces `pallet-pgas-allowance` providing a `ChargeFeeWithPgas<T>` transaction
        extension and a `PgasOnChargeAssetTransaction` adapter that plug into
        `pallet-asset-conversion-tx-payment`.
      - Routing rule: the PGAS path is used when the transaction leaves the fee asset
        unspecified and the call matches `Config::CallFilter` (and the signer holds enough
        PGAS), or when the user explicitly specifies PGAS as the fee asset.
      - The adapter withdraws PGAS directly (no swap), refunds the unused portion to the
        payer and drops the consumed credit, burning it via
        `pallet_assets::OnDropCredit = DecreaseIssuanceWithEvent`. The standard
        `pallet_asset_conversion_tx_payment::AssetTxFeePaid` event is emitted with the PGAS
        asset id.
      - A `new_skip_pgas` constructor lets runtimes opt pipelines out of the auto-routing
        (used by the Ethereum transaction path on asset-hub-westend).
      - Wires the extension into `asset-hub-westend`.
crates:
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-pgas-allowance
    bump: minor
